[b]A mod for Mount & Blade II: Bannerlord.[/b]

Made by two of us: the code and all technical work by Claude (Opus 5.5), an AI; the idea, feedback and playtesting by [url=https://github.com/TraxData313]Trax[/url], Bible believer and engineer in AI/ML/Python/Applied Maths.

[b]Equip anything - earn its full power.[/b]

Skill requirements become soft. Your heroes can equip any weapon, shield, armour, bow or horse. If their skill is below what the item asks for, the requirement shows red in the inventory and they fight with it worse: weaker and slower swings, a shield that breaks sooner, heavy feet in armour, a bow that shoots weak and wide, a horse that answers the reins badly.

[b]An item a tier or two above your skill comes out worse than the one you have mastered.[/b] Troops are never touched.

[h1]What asks for what[/h1]
[list]
[*]Melee weapons: the skill of the way you hold them. Javelins and throwing axes: Throwing when thrown.
[*]Shields and armour: Athletics. Bows / crossbows / slings: Bow / Crossbow / Throwing. Horses: Riding.
[*]The requirement follows the item's tier: Tier 1 = 20, 2 = 45, 3 = 75, 4 = 100, 5 = 125, 6 = 150, up to 200 for the very best.
[*]Bows, crossbows and horses no longer lock you out: equip them and mount any horse, and pay the penalty instead.
[/list]

[h1]How much it costs[/h1]
[list]
[*]At or above the requirement: no penalty at all.
[*]Just below it the penalty snaps in at Low and grows as your skill falls: Mid at 60% of the requirement, High at 30% and below.
[*]Melee damage -25 / -50 / -75%, swing speed and handling -12.5 / -25 / -37.5%.
[*]Ranged damage -25 / -50 / -75%, draw and reload speed -12.5 / -25 / -37.5%, inaccuracy +25 / +50 / +75%.
[*]Shield damage taken +25 / +50 / +75%. Armour foot speed -20 / -40 / -60%, shared by weight. Horse speed and maneuver -25 / -50 / -75%.
[*]Starter gear: every Tier 1 item costs at most 20% on each stat, so a hero with no skill still has something to learn on.
[/list]

[h1]In the inventory[/h1]
[list]
[*][b]Requires: One Handed 95 (yours 77)[/b] - red when short, green when met.
[*]Stat rows show the value after the penalty, then the vanilla value minus the penalty: [i]Swing Damage: 47 (75-28) Cut[/i].
[*][b]Same culture bonus[/b]: on gear of his own culture a hero's skill counts as skill x 1.2 + 5 (tooltip: "yours 150 +35 Battanian"). Adjustable in MCM.
[*][b]Orange rows[/b]: items above the selected hero's skill are tinted orange in the inventory lists. Vanilla's red still means "can't equip at all".
[/list]

[h1]Good to know[/h1]
[list]
[*]Who pays: you, your clan's heroes and every other hero - each a toggle, all on; tournaments and training fights each a toggle, off. [b]Troops never[/b]: vanilla, locks included.
[*]Every number is a setting in Mod Configuration Menu (optional). Without it the mod runs on the defaults.
[*]Works with Trax Combat Enhancements and other mods that change the combat models: the penalties stack on top.
[*]The tooltip uses your plain skill; battle uses the effective skill, so a battle can be a few points kinder.
[/list]

[h1]Requirements[/h1]
[list]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2859188632]Harmony[/url]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2859238197]Mod Configuration Menu[/url] (optional)
[/list]
Works with or without War Sails. For Bannerlord v1.5.7. Safe to add or remove mid-campaign.

Free and open — public domain (The Unlicense). Do whatever you like with it.
